<http://purl.org/spar/bido/ResearchCareerCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bibliometric data that includes categories describing the research career of people. Each of such categories is characterised by four specific dimensions: the research period considered, the curve of the chosen citation distribution, the slope of such curve, and the order of magnitude of the citation of such research period."@en .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/Curve> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The specific shape proper to the clusters identified by the algorithm, which is characterised by a trend (flat/increasing/decreasing) and, in the latter two cases, by an acceleration or deceleration point (none or premature, median, overdue acceleration/deceleration)."@en .
